    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d236">

                <pb facs="0305" n="1039" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1039"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gibbs to Mr.
                            Evarts.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-01-22"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22, 1879</hi></date>.
                        (Received Feb. 15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 300.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to dispatch No.
                    268, of July 24 last, relative to the claims of Messrs. Sparrow, Noland, Gait,
                    and others for moneys due them from the Peruvian Government for their services
                    as members of the late Hydrographic Commission on the Amazon.</p>
                <p>I have kept the claims in view and nowinform you that I have received a
                    communication from the minister of foreign affairs, of which I inclose copy,
                    notifying me that the sums due will be paid through the Peruvian Government’s
                    agents at New York. Mr. Lee, attorney for Mr. Sparrow, wrote to me on the matter
                    last December.</p>
                <p>I have answered the note inclosed, referring him to the Department for further
                    information.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Gibbs.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d236-a1.xml" xpointer="d236-a1"/>
            </div>
